  "issue": {
    "body": "In our case we're streaming in-flight uploaded files directly to MongoDB GridFS,\r\nso if we lose/crash some asgi worker process that is actually using the uploaded yet unprocessed file, a schedule job can detect this and resume operation. With `SpooledTemporaryFile` this is impossible because we can't guarantee that resume job will land in the same container.\r\n\r\nThis all works well with Starlette, only drawback is that we need to monkey-patch `UploadedFile` class with our implementation, that sends chunks to Mongo's `GridFS`.\r\n\r\nCan Startlette have `UploadedFile` class configurable?",
    "closed_at": "2022-02-16T12:32:48Z",
    "created_at": "2019-10-29T12:46:51Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/697",
    "labels": [
      "feature"
    ],
    "number": 697,
    "state": "closed",
    "title": "Add option to overwrite UploadFile impl",
    "user": "canni"
  },
